# Build context exclusions for the AER runtime image.
#
# Two rules drive this file:
#   1. no data and no secrets may ever enter an image -- once pushed, an image is
#      effectively immortal and readable by anyone with pull rights
#      (docs/DECISIONS.md D-038);
#   2. the four things the runtime actually needs must survive: `aer/`,
#      `migrations/`, `alembic.ini` and `scripts/`.
# Root-anchored patterns use a leading `/` so a future directory named `data`
# somewhere inside the package is not silently dropped from the build.
# Everything listed below is noise that only makes the build cache worse.

# --- version control and CI -------------------------------------------------
/.git
/.github
/.gitignore

# --- local environments and tool caches -------------------------------------
/.venv
/venv
/env
/build
/dist
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
/.pytest_cache
/.mypy_cache
/.ruff_cache

# --- data: never baked into an image ----------------------------------------
/data
/backups
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite

# --- secrets: never baked into an image -------------------------------------
# `deploy/` holds the host-side compose file and the production `.env`; mounting
# it into an image would be the fastest way to leak a credential.
/deploy
.env
.env.*
*.env

# --- host-side concerns, docs and the test suite ----------------------------
/docs
/tests
/agent.md
/.workbuddy
*.md
!README.md

# --- editors / OS ------------------------------------------------------------
/.idea
/.vscode
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
